From d9e74d5b305fe752c63af32bb2a64a30daa4e043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:38:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(client): configure printers and print labels from
 the server

Adds a Printers section to Settings (create, edit, delete, set default,
test reachability, and discover the queues an existing CUPS server offers),
and a second print button on the label page that sends the labels to the
configured printer instead of opening the browser's print dialog.

Labels are still rendered by the existing designer via renderLabelDataUrl():
only the destination of the finished raster changes, so the designer stays
the single source of truth for how a label looks.

The new button is rendered only when at least one printer is configured, so
nothing changes for anyone who does not use this. Labels are sent one at a
time and a failure on one does not stop the rest; the outcome is summarised
in a toast.
